abstract: >-
  Research pilot measuring how well Brazilian Portuguese phenotype terms map to the Human
  Phenotype Ontology (HPO) when only English labels are searched, how much of published
  rare-disease case descriptions already has an official Portuguese HPO label, and whether
  small local LLMs extract HPO terms from Portuguese clinical text better directly or after
  translating it to English (synthetic vignettes). Research support only; not a clinical or
  diagnostic tool.
keywords:
  - Human Phenotype Ontology
  - Brazilian Portuguese
  - rare diseases
  - phenotype normalization
  - sentence embeddings
  - phenopackets
  - large language models
  - phenotype extraction
